@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage using native Web Components. No build step or runtime dependencies are required. The page loads `components/daily-grind.js` as a browser module; individual component modules can also be imported separately.
+
+## Component content
+
+Content stays in the page as semantic HTML, remains readable without JavaScript, and can be updated without rebuilding a component. Each component has an open shadow root containing its template and styles.
+
+| Element | Named slots | Default slot |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `coffee-card` | `heading`, `action` | Description |
+| `grind-hero` | `heading`, `action` | Introductory content |
+| `grind-navigation` | `brand` | Navigation links |
+| `grind-footer` | `links` | Copyright or other footer content |
+
+```html
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="heading">House Blend</h3>
+  <p>A balanced roast with chocolate notes.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/house-blend"
+     aria-label="View details about House Blend">View Details</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+Use real heading elements at the appropriate level and native anchors for actions that navigate. Provide a descriptive accessible name when repeating link text. Cards and other static hosts do not add tab stops.
+
+Components inherit typography and accept the theme properties `--primary`, `--secondary`, `--accent`, `--text`, and `--component-focus-color`. The hero additionally accepts `--hero-image` (a CSS image value). Shadow containers expose `card`, `hero`, `navigation`, and `footer` parts for deliberate customization via `::part()`.
+
+Navigation accepts anchors as direct children. Below 48rem, its native Menu button toggles the links; Escape closes the disclosure and restores button focus. On larger screens all links are visible. ARIA controls and their targets live in the same shadow root. Event listeners are removed on disconnect and restored on reconnect, so multiple independent navigation instances are supported.
+
+Page-level CSS controls document layout. Component styles, templates, and disclosure behavior live in `components/`. No client-side router is introduced; destination URLs retain their existing behavior.
